{"questions":[{"question_id":"lsbm7sp8","content":"Given below are two statements :<br/><br/>\n<b>Statement (I)</b> : Potassium hydrogen phthalate is a primary standard for standardisation of sodium hydroxide solution.\n<br/><br/>\n<b>Statement (II)</b> : In this titration phenolphthalein can be used as indicator.<br/><br/>\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the <b>most appropriate</b> answer from the options given below :\n","chapter":"practical-organic-chemistry","chapterGroup":"organic-chemistry","country":"in","difficulty":"easy","exam":"jee-main","examGroup":"jee","isBonus":false,"isOutOfSyllabus":false,"languages":["en","hi"],"marks":4,"negMarks":1,"paperId":"jee-main-2024-online-1st-february-morning-shift","paperTitle":"JEE Main 2024 (Online) 1st February Morning Shift","permalink":"given-below-are-two-statements-brbr-bstatement-i-jee-main-chemistry-g6qpn8krfr8gtluj","question":{"en":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"Given below are two statements :<br/><br/>\n<b>Statement (I)</b> : Potassium hydrogen phthalate is a primary standard for standardisation of sodium hydroxide solution.\n<br/><br/>\n<b>Statement (II)</b> : In this titration phenolphthalein can be used as indicator.<br/><br/>\nIn the light of the above statements, choose the <b>most appropriate</b> answer from the options given below :\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are correct"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>Let's examine each statement one by one to choose the most appropriate answer :</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement (I) : Potassium hydrogen phthalate is a primary standard for standardisation of sodium hydroxide solution.</b></p>\n<p>This statement is correct. Potassium hydrogen phthalate (often abbreviated as KHP, with the chemical formula <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.198ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4507.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3308.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is commonly used as a primary standard in titrations because it is pure, stable, non-hygroscopic, and has a high molar mass. It reacts with sodium hydroxide (NaOH) in a stoichiometric reaction, where one mole of KHP reacts with one mole of NaOH. The equation for the reaction is as follows :</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"44.189ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 19531.3 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3308.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4729.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5730.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6618.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7147.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7910.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(9075.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(10353.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(11505.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(12772.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(13661.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(14861.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(15749.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(16500.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(17500.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(18768.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p><b>Statement (II) : In this titration phenolphthalein can be used as indicator.</b></p>\n<p>This statement is also correct. Phenolphthalein is a suitable indicator for the titration between KHP and NaOH. It changes color in the pH range of about 8.2 to 10, which is appropriate for the endpoint of a titration involving a weak acid (KHP) and a strong base (NaOH). In an acidic solution, phenolphthalein is colorless, but it turns pink in a basic solution, signaling the end of the titration when slight excess NaOH is present.</p>\n\n<p>Given that both statements are correct, the most appropriate answer is :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Option A : Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.</li>\n</ul>"},"hi":{"comprehension":null,"direction":null,"content":"नीचे दो कथन दिए गए हैं :<br/><br/>\n<b>कथन (I)</b> : पोटेशियम हाइड्रोजन फथैलेट सोडियम हाइड्रोक्साइड समाधान के मानकीकरण के लिए प्राथमिक मानक है।\n<br/><br/>\n<b>कथन (II)</b> : इस प्रतिक्रिया में फेनॉलफ्थेलीन का उपयोग संकेतक के रूप में किया जा सकता है।<br/><br/>\nउपरोक्त कथनों के आधार पर, नीचे दिए गए विकल्पों में से <b>सबसे उचित</b> उत्तर का चयन करें :\n","options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों सही हैं"},{"identifier":"B","content":"कथन I गलत है लेकिन कथन II सही है"},{"identifier":"C","content":"कथन I और कथन II दोनों ही गलत हैं"},{"identifier":"D","content":"कथन I सही है लेकिन कथन II गलत है"}],"correct_options":["A"],"answer":null,"explanation":"<p>आइए सबसे उपयुक्त उत्तर चुनने के लिए प्रत्येक कथन की एक-एक करके जांच करें:</p>\n\n<p><b>कथन (I) : पोटैशियम हाइड्रोजन फ्थैलेट सोडियम हाइड्रॉक्साइड विलयन के मानकीकरण के लिए एक प्राथमिक मानक है।</b></p>\n<p>यह कथन सही है। पोटैशियम हाइड्रोजन फ्थैलेट (जिसे अक्सर KHP के रूप में संक्षिप्त किया जाता है, रासायनिक सूत्र <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.198ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4507.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3308.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container> के साथ) आमतौर पर अनुमापन में प्राथमिक मानक के रूप में उपयोग किया जाता है क्योंकि यह शुद्ध, स्थिर, अनार्द्रताग्राही है, और उच्च मोलर द्रव्यमान रखता है। यह सोडियम हाइड्रॉक्साइड (NaOH) के साथ एक रससमीकरणमितीय अभिक्रिया में प्रतिक्रिया करता है, जहां KHP का एक मोल NaOH के एक मोल के साथ अभिक्रिया करता है। अभिक्रिया का समीकरण निम्नानुसार है:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"44.189ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 19531.3 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3308.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4729.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5730.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6618.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7147.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7910.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(9075.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(10353.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(11505.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(12772.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(13661.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(14861.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(15749.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(16500.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(17500.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(18768.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p><b>कथन (II) : इस अनुमापन में फिनॉलफ्थेलीन को सूचक के रूप में उपयोग किया जा सकता है।</b></p>\n<p>यह कथन भी सही है। फिनॉलफ्थेलीन KHP और NaOH के बीच अनुमापन के लिए एक उपयुक्त सूचक है। यह लगभग 8.2 से 10 की pH परास में रंग बदलता है, जो एक दुर्बल अम्ल (KHP) और एक प्रबल क्षार (NaOH) से जुड़े अनुमापन के अंत बिंदु के लिए उपयुक्त है। अम्लीय विलयन में, फिनॉलफ्थेलीन रंगहीन होता है, लेकिन यह क्षारीय विलयन में गुलाबी हो जाता है, जो अनुमापन के अंत का संकेत देता है जब थोड़ी अधिक मात्रा में NaOH उपस्थित होता है।</p>\n\n<p>यह देखते हुए कि दोनों कथन सही हैं, सबसे उपयुक्त उत्तर है:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>विकल्प A : कथन I और कथन II दोनों सही हैं।</li>\n</ul>"}},"subject":"chemistry","timeAllotted":120000,"topic":"chemistry-involved-in-titrimetric-experiments","type":"mcq","year":2024,"tags":["assertion_reason"],"yearKey":"jee-main-2024-online-1st-february-morning-shift","active":true,"options":[{"identifier":"A","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are correct"},{"identifier":"B","content":"Statement I is incorrect but Statement II is correct"},{"identifier":"C","content":"Both Statement I and Statement II are incorrect"},{"identifier":"D","content":"Statement I is correct but Statement II is incorrect"}],"correct_options":["A"],"explanation":"<p>Let's examine each statement one by one to choose the most appropriate answer :</p>\n\n<p><b>Statement (I) : Potassium hydrogen phthalate is a primary standard for standardisation of sodium hydroxide solution.</b></p>\n<p>This statement is correct. Potassium hydrogen phthalate (often abbreviated as KHP, with the chemical formula <mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"10.198ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 4507.7 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3308.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container>) is commonly used as a primary standard in titrations because it is pure, stable, non-hygroscopic, and has a high molar mass. It reacts with sodium hydroxide (NaOH) in a stoichiometric reaction, where one mole of KHP reacts with one mole of NaOH. The equation for the reaction is as follows :</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax\" jax=\"SVG\" overflow=\"overflow\"><svg style=\"vertical-align: -0.375ex;\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"44.189ex\" height=\"1.97ex\" role=\"img\" focusable=\"false\" viewBox=\"0 -705 19531.3 870.6\" xmlns:xlink=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink\"><g stroke=\"currentColor\" fill=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"0\" transform=\"scale(1,-1)\"><g data-mml-node=\"math\"><g data-mml-node=\"msub\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(1151.6,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"35\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-35\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(2419.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(3308.1,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(4729.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(5730.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(6618.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7147.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(7910.1,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(9075.9,0)\"><use data-c=\"2192\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2192\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(10353.7,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D436\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D436\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(748,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"38\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-38\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(11505.2,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(12772.8,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D43E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(13661.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(796,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"34\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-34\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(14861.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D441\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D441\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(15749.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D44E\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D44E\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mo\" transform=\"translate(16500.5,0)\"><use data-c=\"2B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-2B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"msub\" transform=\"translate(17500.8,0)\"><g data-mml-node=\"mi\"><use data-c=\"1D43B\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D43B\"></use></g><g data-mml-node=\"mn\" transform=\"translate(864,-150) scale(0.707)\"><use data-c=\"32\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-N-32\"></use></g></g><g data-mml-node=\"mi\" transform=\"translate(18768.3,0)\"><use data-c=\"1D442\" xlink:href=\"#MJX-TEX-I-1D442\"></use></g></g></g></svg></mjx-container></p>\n\n<p><b>Statement (II) : In this titration phenolphthalein can be used as indicator.</b></p>\n<p>This statement is also correct. Phenolphthalein is a suitable indicator for the titration between KHP and NaOH. It changes color in the pH range of about 8.2 to 10, which is appropriate for the endpoint of a titration involving a weak acid (KHP) and a strong base (NaOH). In an acidic solution, phenolphthalein is colorless, but it turns pink in a basic solution, signaling the end of the titration when slight excess NaOH is present.</p>\n\n<p>Given that both statements are correct, the most appropriate answer is :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Option A : Both Statement I and Statement II are correct.</li>\n</ul>"}]}